{"id":"word:hebrew:H3001","type":"word","title":"יָבֵשׁ","subtitle":"H3001 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be ashamed , confused or disappointed ; also (as failing) to dry up (as water) or wither (as herbage)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יָבֵשׁ (H3001) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 73 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יָבֵשׁ (yâbêsh) means to be ashamed , confused or disappointed ; also (as failing) to dry up (as water) or wither (as herbage) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 13 4."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יָבֵשׁ","transliteration":"yâbêsh","pronunciation":"yaw-bashe'","strong":"H3001","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3001","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["הֹבִ֥ישׁ","יָבֵ֖שׁ","תִּיבָֽשׁ","תִּיבָ֔שׁ","הֹבִ֖ישָׁה"],"morphs":[["HVhp3ms",12],["HVqp3ms",9],["HVqi3fs",5],["HVhp3fs",5],["HVqp3cp",4],["HC/Vqw3ms",3],["HC/Vqq3ms",3],["HVqi3ms",3],["HVhi1cs",3],["HVhp3cp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be ashamed , confused or disappointed ; also (as failing) to dry up (as water) or wither (as herbage)","usage":"be ashamed, clean, be confounded, (make) dry (up), (do) shame(-fully), × utterly, wither (away).","full":"H3001. yabesh I. יָבֵשׁ verb be dry, dried up, withered (Late Hebrew id. (rare), יְבֵישׁ ᵑ7 , chiefly Pa`al, Ithpe`el, Syriac ; Sabean, Palmyrene derivatives; Arabic ; Ethiopic ) — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular יָבֵשׁ Josh 9:5 8 t.; וְיָבֵשׁ consecutive Isa 19:5 + 4 t.; 3 feminine singular יָבְשָׁה Gen 8:14 ; 3 plural יָבְשׁוּ Jer 23:10 2 t.; יָבֵ֑שׁוּ 50:38 2 t.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִבַשׁ Isa 19:7 ; יִיבָ֑שׁ Jer 12:4 ; Job 8:12 ; וַיִּיבַשׁ 1Kin 17:7 ; וַיִּיבָ֑שׁ Jonah 4:7 ; 3 feminine singular תִּיבַשׁ Ezek 17:10 ; תִּיבָ֑שׁ 17:10 3 t., etc.; Infinitive construct (בִּ)יבשׁ Isa 27:11 ; יְבשֶׁת Gen 8:7 ; absolute יָבוֺשׁ Zech 11:17 ; יָבשׁ Eccl 17:10; &#8212; 1 be dry, dried up without moisture: a. of bread Josh 9:5 , 12 (JE). b. of ground lacking rain Amos 4:7 , compare 1:2 (of Carmel at utterance of ׳י s voice), Jer 23:10 . c. of earth after the flood Gen 8:14 (P), compare חָרֵב d. of grass, herbage , trees and crops (already implied in b. = wither Isa 15:6 ; 19:7 ; 27:11 ; Jer 12:4 ; Job 8:12 ; Joel 1:12 ; Jonah 4:7 ; in simile of shortness of life Psa 90:6 ; 102:12 ; 129:6 , see also Isa 40:7-8 , (in these two || נָבֵל ); of heart under figure of grass Psa 102:5 ; of Judah under figure of vine Ezek 17:9 (twice in verse); 17:10 (3 t. in verse), compare 19:12 ; of princes under figure of tree Isa 40:24 ; of roots of Ephraim under figure of tree Hosea 9:16 , so of roots of wicked Job 18:16 . e. of hand, arm , dry up, wither , as judgment from ׳י , 1Kin 13:4 ; Zech 11:17 (twice in verse); in distress כֹּחִי כַּחֶרֶשׁ יָבֵשׁ Psa 22:16 my strength is dried up like the potsherd ; of skin Lam 4:8 , and (figurative) of bones Ezek 37:11 . 2 be dried up: of water Gen 8:7 (J), Isa 19:5 ; 1Kin 17:7 ; Jer 50:38 ; Joel 1:20 ; Job 12:15 ; 14:11 . Pi`el make dry, dry up , only Imperfect 3masculine singular suffix וַיַּבְּשֵׁהוּ Nahum 1:4 and hath made it dry ( ׳י , the sea); 3 feminine singular תְּיַבֵּשׁ Job 15:30 the flame shall dry up his branches (figurative of wicked); figurative תְּיַבֶּשׁנָּֿ֑רֶם Prov 17:22 a broken spirit maketh dry ( the ) bones. Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular הוֺבִישׁ Josh 2:10 3 t. + Joel 1:10 (see below); חֹבִישׁ Ezek 19:12 2 t. Joel (see below); 3feminine singular הוֺבִישָׁה Joel 1:12 (see below); 2 masculine singular הוֺבַשְׁתָּ Psa 74:15 ; 1 singular הוֺבַשְׁתִּי Ezek 17:24 ; וְהוֺבַשְׁתִּ֫י Jer 51:36 ; 3 plural וְהֹבִישׁוּ consecutive Zech 10:11 ; Imperfect 1singular אוֺבִישׁ Isa 42:15 (twice in verse); 44:27 ; &#8212; dry up, make dry: 1 dry up water , ׳י subject, Josh 2:10 ; 4:23 (twice in verse); 5:1 (all D), Jer 51:36 (|| הֶחֱרִיב ), Isa 42:15 ; 44:27 ( חֳרָבִי in || clause), Psa 74:15 . 2 make dry, wither: herbage, trees, crops, etc., of ׳י , Isa 42:15 (|| החריב ); object Babylon under figure of tree Ezek 17:24 ; of east wind's drying up Judah's fruit 19:12 . 3 exhibit dryness: of river-deeps laid bare Zech 10:11 . &#8212; In like manner might be taken Joel 1:10 , 12 (twice in verse); 1:17 , if from יבשׁ ; but the sense would be difficult, especially in 1:10 ; 1:12 , and הֹבִישׁוּ 1:11 must be from בּוֺשׁ , to which all these cases in Joel may be consistently assigned; see בּוֺשׁ .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 13 4","keyReferences":["1Kgs 13 4","1Kgs 17 7","2Sam 19 6","Amos 1 2","Amos 4 7","Ezek 17 9","Ezek 17 9","Ezek 17 10"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":73,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 13 4","book":"1Kgs","chapter":13,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תִּיבַ֤שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3fs"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 7","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּיבַ֣שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"2Sam 19 6","book":"2Sam","chapter":19,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֹבַ֨שְׁתָּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhp2ms"},{"reference":"Amos 1 2","book":"Amos","chapter":1,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יָבֵ֖שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqp3ms"},{"reference":"Amos 4 7","book":"Amos","chapter":4,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּיבָֽשׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3fs"},{"reference":"Ezek 17 9","book":"Ezek","chapter":17,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יָבֵ֗שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq3ms"},{"reference":"Ezek 17 9","book":"Ezek","chapter":17,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּיבָ֔שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3fs"},{"reference":"Ezek 17 10","book":"Ezek","chapter":17,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּיבַ֣שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3fs"},{"reference":"Ezek 17 10","book":"Ezek","chapter":17,"verse":10,"